1️⃣ Client requests token from OAuth server
      ↓
2️⃣ OAuth server issues access token to client
      ↓
3️⃣ Client calls API:
      Authorization: Bearer <token>
      ↓
4️⃣ Request hits Akamai (edge/CDN/WAF)
      ↓
5️⃣ Akamai forwards request to API Gateway
      ↓
6️⃣ API Gateway validates token with OAuth server (or locally, if JWT)
      ↓
7️⃣ If valid, API Gateway routes request to the service in Kubernetes pod
      ↓
8️⃣ Pod executes the service layer logic and returns response